fleet-worker@.service is a systemd template unit. Install it once per box:

  sudo cp /opt/fleet/fleet/systemd/fleet-worker@.service /etc/systemd/system/
  sudo systemctl daemon-reload
  sudo systemctl enable --now fleet-worker@<instance>

<instance> picks the env file /etc/fleet/<instance>.env (mode 0600, owner root:fleet, 0640).
Use the role name as the instance (ads, quotes, scheduler, followup, host) so
`journalctl -u fleet-worker@quotes` reads naturally. FLEET_ROLE inside the file is what counts.

Logs:    journalctl -u fleet-worker@quotes -f
Status:  systemctl status fleet-worker@quotes
Restart: sudo systemctl restart fleet-worker@quotes   (after a git pull or env change)

The unit runs as the unprivileged `fleet` user with a read-only /opt/fleet and a private /tmp.
Full setup: /opt/fleet/fleet/README.md.
